            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "sections/cper-section-nvidia.c",
                    "line": 206,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Lets model this like we do the other one:\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/libcper/blob/043d5f4b4f95d9f2a4f8182850ed0e6f2b076b15/cper-utils.c#L453\n\n1. If the value matches, use it directly (so unit tests still pass even with fuzzing enabled), and we're only modifying the failure path.\n2. Put it in a helper function.\n3. Make sure we're using something from the input buffer to do it, so the fuzzer can hit everything.  Generally we would just use the first character and mod it into an index."
                },
                {
                    "file": "sections/cper-section-nvidia.c",
                    "line": 206,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aushim Nagarkatti",
                        "email": "aush281@gmail.com",
                        "username": "aushimnagarkatti"
                    },
                    "message": "1. I don't follow what directly means here. You don't want `nv_signature` to exist?\n2. Helper function common to any fuzzing path in the file, or just for this specific scenario?\n3. we're using size from the input here"
                },
                {
                    "file": "sections/cper-section-nvidia.c",
                    "line": 206,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> 1. I don't follow what directly means here. You don't want `nv_signature` to exist?\n\nI mean, keep the code path the same for \"normal\" cases.  Only call the fuzz specific path if the main path \"fails\" to find a match.\n\n> 2. Helper function common to any fuzzing path in the file, or just for this specific scenario?\n\nThis specific scenario is fine.  Just want to abstract away the \"get an index\" so this is readable.\n\n> 3. we're using size from the input here'\n\nSize isn't a field though, it's the total lenth.  There are conditions where you have a bug, but you never hit it because the size that fails isn't of mod(code index)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "sections/cper-section-nvidia.c",
                    "line": 206,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
